<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11096" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄξων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ονος</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>axle,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				16.378
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σιδήρεος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					5.723
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φήγινος</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				838
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				424
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				153
			</span></i> (lyr.), etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>axis,</i> of a cone, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				375b22
			</span></i>; of a conic section, <i><span class="en">
				Apollon.Perg.
				1
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Def.</u>
				7
			</span></i>; of a cylinder, <i><span class="en">
				Archim.
				<u>Con.Sph.</u>
				1.260
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>axis of the celestial sphere,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mu.</u>
				391b26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				2.5
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. νοητός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eust.
					1389.59
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> metaph.,
				<i>course, path</i> of action, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Pr.</u>
				2.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.18
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἄξονες</span>
			<i>the wooden tablets of the laws</i> in Athens, <i>made to turn
				upon an axis,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Sol.</u>
				25
			</span></i>: sg. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				1.61
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				23.31
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in pl.,
				<i>door-jambs,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Parm.
				1.19
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> in pl.,
				<i>part of a bridle-bit,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				10.9
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>the second cervical vertebra,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				2.132
			</span></i>. (Cf. Skt. <i>ák[snull ]as,</i> Lat.
				<i>axis,</i> OHG. <i>ahsa,</i> Lith.
				<i>ašìs</i> 'axle'.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>